# No Git LFS.
#
# This used to route *.bin through LFS, which covers the world chunk files --
# moshpit/server/universe/**/*.region.bin, about 80 MB across 40 files. They are
# committed as ordinary blobs instead: LFS would need git-lfs installed on every
# clone plus quota (GitHub's free tier is 1 GB, and re-adding the world costs
# 80 MB each time), and the world changes rarely enough that plain git is fine.
#
# Leaving the rule in place while the files were already committed as blobs was
# the actual hazard: the next `git add` on a machine WITH git-lfs would rewrite
# them as pointers and produce a mixed history.

# Binary. Never normalise line endings in these.
*.bin      -text
*.png      -text
*.ogg      -text
*.zip      -text
*.blockymodel  -text
*.blockyanim   -text
